{
  "about": "How bytes a caller hands the boundary are read (CONTRACT §0), as one list of cases: base64url, forgiving the padding and the standard alphabet's + and /, and nothing else. A character outside the alphabet — whitespace of any kind included — a last character with a spare bit set, `=` anywhere but the end and a length that leaves one character over are refused as {parse, not base64url}. The members of an envelope that travelled are read by a stricter rule still (CONTRACT §5). The core's test (crates/hdtp-identity/src/util.rs, arguments_are_read_as_one_list_says) and the Go port's (go/b64_test.go, TestArgumentsAreReadAsOneListSays) read it. A case answers `hex`, or `refused`.",
  "cases": [
    {"name": "nothing", "in": "", "hex": ""},
    {"name": "three bytes", "in": "AQID", "hex": "010203"},
    {"name": "two bytes", "in": "AQI", "hex": "0102"},
    {"name": "one byte", "in": "AQ", "hex": "01"},
    {"name": "padded", "in": "AQ==", "hex": "01"},
    {"name": "padded short", "in": "AQ=", "hex": "01"},
    {"name": "padded long", "in": "AQ===", "hex": "01"},
    {"name": "the standard alphabet", "in": "+/8", "hex": "fbff"},
    {"name": "the url alphabet", "in": "-_8", "hex": "fbff"},
    {"name": "the two alphabets mixed", "in": "+-_/", "hex": "fbefff"},
    {"name": "a space", "in": "A Q", "refused": true},
    {"name": "a tab", "in": "A\tQ", "refused": true},
    {"name": "a line feed", "in": "A\nQ", "refused": true},
    {"name": "CR LF", "in": "A\r\nQ", "refused": true},
    {"name": "spaces around", "in": " AQ ", "refused": true},
    {"name": "padding then a line feed", "in": "AQ==\n", "refused": true},
    {"name": "a line feed inside the padding", "in": "AQ=\n=", "refused": true},
    {"name": "one character over", "in": "A", "refused": true},
    {"name": "five characters", "in": "AQIDB", "refused": true},
